{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers","id":1419868,"title":"Euthanatos killers, gamblers, no school-teachers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-23T17:26:16-07:00","id":1419868,"title":"Euthanatos killers, gamblers, no school-teachers?","content":"The Euthanatos, as they are presented, remind me of janitorial staff carrying away garbage slower than the rate at which it is being dumped on them. They are supposed to be guiding people through multiple incarnations, helping them achieve the divine purpose assigned to them by higher powers.<br /> <br /> In practice, as they are depicted and commonly played as characters, they seek out people who are spiritually corrupt, past the point of redemption, and kill them. &quot;Society produces all these malignant souls who have fallen short of their Dharma. It's my job to eliminate those idiots before they harm anyone... because I dig Hinduism. It's where it's at.&quot;, says the murder-hobo who just killed all your most original, thoughtful NPCs.<br /> <br /> Why are there no Euthanatos involved in early childhood education? Wouldn't that be the most efficient way of steering people towards their Dharma. A school teacher comes in contact with newly incarnated souls at a time where there is the most opportunity to inspire them toward the good.<br /> <br /> Less hit men. More teachers.<br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T17:29:51-07:00","id":1419870,"title":"","content":"Have you read the revised tradition book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T17:47:18-07:00","id":1419874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419870#post1419870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read the revised tradition book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I basically mine the books for information essential to my chronicle, like the sub-factions. I read the &quot;Famous Euthanatos&quot; and sample characters near the end. The one I remember is a woman whose son gets into trouble. She fails to intervein, loses her son and then realizes she should have killed the people who lead him astray - something like that. I was looking for a template or character who vaguely resembles a school teacher or plays a similar role. If you know of one, do tell.<br /> <br /> What is your interpretation of Euthanatos revised?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 09-30-2021, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T17:49:07-07:00","id":1419875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419874#post1419874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is your interpretation of Euthanatos revised?</div> </div> </div> </div>That anyone who thinks they are nothing more then killers or gamblers needs to read it cover to cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T18:03:30-07:00","id":1419880,"title":"","content":"The common Euthanatoi/Chakravanti stereotype is that of a serial killer inspired by vaguely eastern mysticism, true enough, but this has never been the best presentation of the tradition, even when it was what White Wolf itself was somewhat preoccupied with.<br /> <br /> Any paradigm that does not explicitly call for pacifism will have ideological room within their ranks for militant and violent practitioners. From the Templar of the Celestial Choir, the Executioner Priests of the Verbenae, or too one particularly radical Etherite that uses the psychic energy of human suffering to power their creations; every tradition has room for dark and bloody elements. The Chakravanti have simply been burdened with the archetype more then others.<br /> <br /> The Chakravanti are dedicated to a variety of cyclical concepts which are perhaps best exemplified by eastern philosophies such as Karma, Dharma, and the like. They are not limited to the Vedic sphere though as numerous philosophies have embraced enough precepts of reincarnation, cyclical existence, and the persistence of energy through the churning of entropic wheels. Wherever such philosophy exist (particularly alongside sympathy for the mystical) there will be a place for the Chakravanti.<br /> <br /> The philosophies that form this tradition\u2018s core are mystically nuanced and are often misunderstood, particularly in the west where they are foreign. I am not an expert either and thus everything I say on the topic should be taken with a grain of salt, as well as everything I say in general. I am, after all, a stranger on the internet.<br /> <br /> The Chakravanti are concerned with the cycles of life and existence. Things come to be, exist, and are cycled back by entropy. Perhaps their is an escape from this, perhaps not. Regardless the cycle occurs and human souls (alongside the matter that make up the physical vessels) will go through this process. As people live they accumulate karmic drag which may drift them closer towards harmony or towards corruption.<br /> <br /> Those who are truly corrupt have become stuck in the wheel, disturbing the whole revolution and thus threatening every other soul. Because of their concern for the wheel itself (and the greatest number of souls) the Chakravanti must sometimes, tragically, remove a soiled bit of chaff from the wheel and return it to the cycle so that not only will the wheel turn unhindered again but that the soul will have a chance to redeem itself and live a new and better life.<br /> <br /> This is how it is meant to be but not entirely as it is, because the world we live in is full of corruption and material chaff clogging the wheels of the universe. This is a cause of concern for everything but the Chakravanti know that only they understand it truly. The dire straits and isolation cause some to become radical, acting more and more judiciously as they choose those who must be slain to cleanse the wheel. Many who walk this path without understanding will risk falling to the darkness of the nephandic path.<br /> <br /> Yet this is a tragic extreme and does not represent the whole. The Chakravanti can be found in every walk of life and while their philosophy is somewhat regionally bound, the global environment allows them to fulfill their duties anywhere. They are teachers, gurus, historians, journalists, and social workers alongside so much else.<br /> <br /> They are Awakened. Whatever form they take, their lives are never inconsequential, and as Chakravanti they shall always seek to bring harmony to the wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T19:37:03-07:00","id":1419894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419875#post1419875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That anyone who thinks they are nothing more then killers or gamblers needs to read it cover to cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Opinion = killers <br /> Obligation = Read Euthanatos cover to cover (Friday night when I'm researching other stuff with seven tabs open and writing in time for my chronicle session)<br /> <br /> My own opinion is not that they ARE only killers and gamblers. As a storyteller, I form my own interpretation of them, which IS based on having read most of Revised. If I am reading a novel that I intend to read to the end, I can get into expository dialogue. If it is a book that is supposed to be delivering information in a compact way, my brain throws the expository dialogue in the recycle bin. The book is saying there are two people debating killing a man for horrific crimes against children - a contrivance to justify .. being a killer. Recycle bin. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers#post1419868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practice, as they are depicted and commonly played as characters, they seek out people who are spiritually corrupt, past the point of redemption, and kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the gaming table, in my past experience, they were played as killers. I quit playing Mage because all my NPCs were dead. All the players wanted to do was shoot the technomancer and steal his Node. The group I left still plays that way, when they play Mage. After almost two decades, I started storytelling for two complete newbies who now love Mage because of how I tell the story. I hold my players in deep regard for treating the work I do on NPCs and setting with respect. There are already story circumstances that force them to consider killing an antagonist, but they face the normal psychological side effects of committing murder, if the do. Mages are human, after all. <br /> <br /> I have plans to include Wraith and Changeling crossovers, in that order. Given the time, I will read Wraith Core and watch the rest of &quot;Life Derailed&quot; on YouTube. I have a Euthanatos NPC, already made, who is tied to the Wraith plot-thread. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T19:58:26-07:00","id":1419898,"title":"","content":"This... really doesn't sound like it has anything to do with the Euthanatos, but with you having a bad experience due to a disconnect with a group in terms of expectations and social contract.<br /> <br /> If you think the Euthanatos are a vital element to a group that wants to play violent mages who want to take an excuse they can to kill NPCs... all I can do is say you can make &quot;murder-hobo&quot; mages of any Tradition.<br /> <br /> Also remember that all of your &quot;original, thoughful NPCs,&quot; are just stat blocks with a bunch of expository dialogue that they just threw in the recycle bin. It seems very strange to resist the idea of reading the Revised Traditionbook cover to cover (they're not that long) because you're going to ignore stuff, while also being frustrated that your former players didn't feel like waiting around for you to reveal how cool your NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T21:11:14-07:00","id":1419908,"title":"","content":"The Euthanatos are also teachers, but they aren't as deeply invested in needing to control formal educational institutions to the extent that other Mage groups are. The Celestial Chorus is deeply tied into the world's religions and it's much easier to make people devoted believers if you get them practicing it when young (and can explain away the stuff that doesn't make sense when they get older). The Order of Hermes needs highly educated people for its base paradigm and they are elitist, so they'd get involved in education to raise up the right portion of Sleepers (not enough energy to raise them all up so each Hermetic would decide who has potential and work there). The Sons of Ether are scientists, so they'd be in science education and the Technocracy needs its technicians.<br /> <br /> Since Euthanatos are about the duty to the Wheel, one could certainly see the modern educational system as a problem and start being a teacher. It reminds me of James Zambrano in his Mage: the Podcast guest appearances. A Native American or Goth (he's a member of both groups in real life) could belong to any faction in the Mage setting. They'll more easily fit better than others, but when you do play a character, take the time to do the homework so you make a real person.<br /> <br /> Bad players can make any character type into a murderhobo, even if the background on the sheet and their prelude say otherwise. Bad players can also show a lack of respect for NPCs. In many types of RPGs, this is rewarded and killing your foes usually ends your conflict with them. It's just a bit easier to make murderhoboes or act like murderhoboes if you don't do the homework.<br /> <br /> I'm glad the OP has players now who want to explore the richness of Mage. There are so many things to do in this game instead of just killing them all and taking their stuff.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T22:25:05-07:00","id":1419917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419898#post1419898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This... really doesn't sound like it has anything to do with the Euthanatos, but with you having a bad experience due to a disconnect with a group in terms of expectations and social contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are true, because the books we had presented them that way and, yes, it has to do with that experience. The term &quot;social contract&quot; did not exist in the context of rp. ( know what it means, generally) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419898#post1419898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think the Euthanatos are a vital element to a group that wants to play violent mages who want to take an excuse they can to kill NPCs... all I can do is say you can make &quot;murder-hobo&quot; mages of any Tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I say Mage needs &quot;goblins&quot;. And, yes, I have read Gods and Monsters. In games like D&amp;D, players who want to kill as many things as they can have a plethora of well establishes monster hierarchies that they can bloody their armor with. I enjoy battle tactics, myself. Mage needs stock monsters that have a low rp-performance requirement from the storyteller and can be killed repeatedly. And this isn't just me complaining and doing nothing about it. I have been putting some thought into creating these. Hollow Earth, low light adventure, an avian realm and more. Original aliens. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419898#post1419898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also remember that all of your &quot;original, thoughful NPCs,&quot; are just stat blocks with a bunch of expository dialogue that they just threw in the recycle bin. It seems very strange to resist the idea of reading the Revised Traditionbook cover to cover (they're not that long) because you're going to ignore stuff, while also being frustrated that your former players didn't feel like waiting around for you to reveal how cool your NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>If an NPC was someone they identified as a quest giver from previous sessions, they would return to this NPC for new orders long after they surpassed that NPC in power. I could insulate a character from meaningless execution by defining them in this role. &quot;I have this mission for you if you're interested.&quot; was as much dialogue as they were interested in. When I was not storytelling, I turned the whole thing on its head by overthrowing a quest-giving duke in a coup. <br /> <br /> There is also an important distinction to be made between players who kill sometimes and the murder-hobo. <br /> <br /> In a reply above, I explained that in my current chronicle, players face the choice of having to kill someone, but with good reason and a weighty decision to be made together. Context: A Technomancer who could not advance in the hierarchy of a nearby construct has set up shop in a Tradition controlled city. They met, discussed some maters and agreed not to tell their respective factions about the other's existence, leaving open the possibility of working together. Perception + empathy rolls indicated that both sides intended to keep the promise at the time it was made. However, something may actually happen that triggers the tech NPC to report the players last known location to technocracy higherups. Should they kill her and cover their tracks? One player is close to her own sleeper family. Do they cross the threshold and kill for the right reason? <br /> <br /> The murder hobo doesn't consider this for more than a second. There is no reason to invest any energy giving this character a personality. The murder hobo trains the storyteller to produce, as you said, stat block sheets. Wits + Alertness, dex + firearms, stamina + body armor. We all know that game. Time 3, &quot;I go first and pop them all.&quot;. Blood in the streets. Players have liberated a new Node.<br /> <br /> At the moment, my time is best served writing more material for my setting and comparing ideas on our forum. Wraith Core is ahead of Euthanatos Revised on my reading list. My Euthanatos NPC will connect the players to a Wraith plot thread, yet to be written. My crossovers are Wraith and Changeling only. <br /> <br /> Tell you what. I will post Prisha Braxton (maiden name is Indian, but I don't have &quot;named characters&quot; on hand). At that time, you can tell me if she does the Euthanatos justice. Griffon15's reply above is a pleasure to read, in case you didn't see it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T00:16:46-07:00","id":1419927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419874#post1419874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I basically mine the books for information essential to my chronicle, like the sub-factions. I read the &quot;Famous Euthanatos&quot; and sample characters near the end. The one I remember is a woman whose son gets into trouble. She fails to intervein, loses her sun and then realizes she should have killed the people who lead him astray - something like that. I was looking for a template or character who vaguely resembles a school teacher or plays a similar role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first, I think you should go back and read that page again, because its conclusions were more nuanced than &quot;the character should have killed the Nazis when she had the chance&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's a character devoted less to killing people - the only explicit reference to the character doing so is in the very last sentence under Equipment (&quot;tiny pistol (just good enough for putting a hole in a hatemonger's head)&quot;) - and more with killing IDEAS. That the freedom to learn is important, but that some ideas are toxic and harmful and need to be fought when they are used to peddle hate and despair. The character is described as spending more time inhibiting the ability of such people to spread their message (often through disabling communications technology or reading their minds to gauge their intent/seriousness).<br /> <br /> I can see this kind of character in the modern day being a kind of breadtuber, undermining the work of reactionaries and grifters through both education and sabotage. Taking away the tools of such people, while giving the general public the intellectual tools to identify such indoctrination methods and fight back against them. Inoculating their minds against the viruses of hateful, reactionary ideology and rhetoric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T00:37:19-07:00","id":1419933,"title":"","content":"Don't read the whole book if you can't, but read the Chodona (their law/belief system). And then have your own NPC high ranking Eutanatoi enforcing it.<br /> <br /> The Chodona traces very strict lines arround *when* (and also how) it's acceptable to kill. Eutanatoi are very hard-liners with delivering the &quot;good death&quot; propperly, because if you start killing people w/o deep deliberation (and, worse, with magick - as mages tend to do) , you get Jhor. And that's very bad.<br /> <br /> Eutanatoi police themselves as readily (and as lethaly), if not more, than they do with random people - because they know the power (and divine rigth) to kill corrupts. Like, a lot.<br /> <br /> There's nothing that can placate the &quot;murder-hobo Eutanatoi syndrome&quot; quite like their own mentors schooling them *hard* on why they shouldn't have that disposition if they want to have a long life, the first time they go on a killing rampage. Or at least that's how *I* got out of it (I had made pretty much a murder-hobo, because I tought that was how they rolled, based on stereotype)<br /> <br /> Well, this is if the player/s *have* choosen to be killers, which as stated ain't necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-24-2020, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T02:26:39-07:00","id":1419948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419917#post1419917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both are true, because the books we had presented them that way and, yes, it has to do with that experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is by the Revised era at least, the books didn't present them that way. Even the Revised core book short splat write-up is rather clear that (1) there's a lot more to them than killing, and (2) they consider killing a sacred duty to be taken with utmost deliberation. Some of this is because the earlier books weren't on-point about this and the Euthanatos murder hobo idea had latched on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The term &quot;social contract&quot; did not exist in the context of rp. ( know what it means, generally) </div> </div> </div>&quot;Did not,&quot; doesn't really seem important compared to the fact that it has been used quite extensively in RPG design talk for at least 20 years. Social contract theory doesn't really get talked about much in gaming books, but it's been on the minds of RPG creators for awhile now. The WoD (largely out of popularity at the time than being particularly unique) was the poster child for a need for better understanding of guiding social contract building as part of what the rules should do precisely because so many people have WoD anecdotes just like the one you presented.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is why I say Mage needs &quot;goblins&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Mage has plenty of low-consequence things to kill for groups that want to focus on that for their fun, they're just low priority things buried deep in various supplements because catering to those players has always been a low priority for the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is also an important distinction to be made between players who kill sometimes and the murder-hobo. </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that there's a much more important distinction to be made between players who kill at whatever level of frequency because it's a positive for the game being playerd, and murder hobos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The murder hobo trains the storyteller to produce, as you said, stat block sheets. </div> </div> </div>So, you missed the main point of what I was saying then.<br /> <br /> They don't &quot;train&quot; STs to do anything. Just like the books don't train you to skip important nuances in them because of your own personal dispositions.<br /> <br /> Players that tend to make murder hobo PCs are expressing specific desires for what they want to do for fun in a game. If you can have fun with the same subject matter, but want to get into deeper issues, you need to engage them where their interests lie; and you have a major advantage over a book because you can change your approach as you're not a fixed text.<br /> <br /> While leaving a group because their approach just isn't compatible for you is a good choice, there's still something to be said for making sure you meet your players where they are. Thoughtfully crafting NPCs need to include hooks that the players will actually care about. All your awesome NPCs getting killed because the players never saw them as useful beyond target practice is at least in part because you didn't make them in a fashion that would have headed off that reaction. NPCs that aren't interesting to the players are NPCs that are going to inspire the players to not value those NPCs as full characters.0<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Griffon15's reply above is a pleasure to read, in case you didn't see it. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I do read the other posts in threads I participate in. There wasn't anything to add to that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T03:47:34-07:00","id":1419956,"title":"","content":"Couldt one be a midwife? They are obsessed with the cycles of LIFE and death and childbirth is part of the wheel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T07:24:28-07:00","id":1419982,"title":"","content":"Some Euthanatos might be teachers. Strict teachers - very strict teachers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T14:51:50-07:00","id":1420026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419956#post1419956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldt one be a midwife? They are obsessed with the cycles of LIFE and death and childbirth is part of the wheel</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, yeah. There's many of examples of medic Euthanatoi because medics have to deal with death and life, and a midwife certainly seems to have a place there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Euthanatos might be teachers. Strict teachers - very strict teachers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> Eutanatoi come from the people in India that dealt with death and dead people, that were regarded as &quot;not persons&quot; (below all castes) by the strict Hindu caste system. As I see them within this context, a lot of their whole deal with the concept of &quot;justice&quot; comes from the perspective of being marginalized, and often misunderstood<br /> <br /> As such, I imagine a Entuanatos teacher it's going to be teaching in the most abject of society. While Hermetics are famous for their involvement in academia, to teach in a public school where the children of the very poor and marginalized go to learn, or maybe in a prision or reformatory - seems like a paralel to Eutanatoi Traditional role, if u want one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T15:04:59-07:00","id":1420028,"title":"","content":"If I were to try and sum up the Euthanatoi in a single word, it would be Psychopomp. While the term - literally &quot;soul conductor&quot; in Ancient Greek - traditionally refers to beings who guide the recently deceased to the afterlife, it has also taken on a more modern meaning as &quot;soul guide&quot; to the living as well as the dead. While this does include the idea of administering &quot;The Good Death&quot; to those in need as a way of preserving the Great Wheel, it also includes healing in the physical, mental and spiritual sense - trying to alleviate the suffering, sadness and shame which can damage the Great Wheel - and helping individuals meet their destined purpose in each life.<br /> <br /> As far as non-assassin/gambler concepts, I'd suggest the following:<ul><li>Fate-wise Matchmaker</li> <li>EMT turned Chooser of the Slain</li> <li>Former gangbanger who &quot;died&quot; at the crossroads (street corner) only to be reborn as a psychopomp for those impacted by inner city gang violence</li> <li>Troubled diviner trying to work out the secrets of her past lives</li> <li>Blues musician haunted by ghosts</li> <li>Powerful matriarch of a well established New Orleans family</li> <li>Thanatoic apologist Herald</li> <li>International financier guided by her ancestors</li> <li>Neighborhood midwife practicing ancient magics</li> <li>Suicide hotline councilor</li> <li>Human rights activist</li> <li>Maiden initiate of an ancient mystery cult</li> <li>Explorer of the Underworld</li> <li>Professional bodyguard</li> <li>Medical doctor ministering to the poor and destitute</li> <li>College professor of advanced mathematics/chaos theory/thermodynamics</li> <li>Sin-Eater who takes on the regrets of the recently dead so that they can pass on</li> <li>Shiavist dance instructor</li> </ul>As for the issue of Murder Hoboing, that was one of the reasons the second edition Tradition book introduced the concept of Jhor, which others have mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-24-2020, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T15:14:25-07:00","id":1420031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419948#post1419948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Did not,&quot; doesn't really seem important compared to the fact that it has been used quite extensively in RPG design talk for at least 20 years. Social contract theory doesn't really get talked about much in gaming books, but it's been on the minds of RPG creators for awhile now. </div> </div> </div> </div>Seth Skorkowsky has a very excellent video on the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KBymJBOjwEc\" target=\"_blank\">Social Contract in RPGs</a>. I recommend it to anyone who hasn't seen it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T19:09:09-07:00","id":1420058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419927#post1419927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well first, I think you should go back and read that page again, because its conclusions were more nuanced than &quot;the character should have killed the Nazis when she had the chance&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the time I read it, I was experiencing Nazi-fatigue. Having just re-read it, there is a lot to draw from. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419927#post1419927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see this kind of character in the modern day being a kind of breadtuber, undermining the work of reactionaries and grifters through both education and sabotage. Taking away the tools of such people, while giving the general public the intellectual tools to identify such indoctrination methods and fight back against them. Inoculating their minds against the viruses of hateful, reactionary ideology and rhetoric.</div> </div> </div> </div>I often see the word &quot;reactionary&quot; used in condemnation of Nazis and other presumably dangerous people, as if reactionism is always incorrect. Reactionaries can be correct. The whole environmental movement is a response to the unknown future variable effect of corporate exploitation of the planet. Environmentalists were constantly being referred to as &quot;crazies&quot; and other such pejoratives. As predicted results increasingly manifest, hurricanes, etc., the phenomenon being reacted to is understood and acknowledged. It is partially the result of collusion between extractive industry and corrupt officials - a conspiracy. Does Al Gore's too-early prediction of sea-level rise make him a grifter? <br /> <br /> In the United States, there is a rather large overlap between people passionate about gun rights and those who agree with the message of (corporate sponsored) global warming denial. As someone who is concerned about the environment, it does not serve me to vilify the guy clinging to his gun and declaring his resistance to his way of life being forcibly changed by the rest of society. I have to consider, for example, what bad things could be perpetrated against a disarmed population by the worst imaginable government. He is reacting to an unknown and can't be faulted for imagining the worst.<br /> <br /> Reactionism can, of course, be a mechanism for the delivery of a destructive ideology - reactionism and bad ideology being separate things. &quot;They are trying to take our guns,&quot; could be true. There are strong arguments for gun control, publicly expressed. &quot;because they are in league with a foreign non-citizen population.&quot; is the ideology's message. The emotion of the first statement impairs analysis of the second. <br /> <br /> Censor has the Mind Sphere - Mind 2. She can read surface thoughts and perfectly understand the emotion of her target. Mage canon acknowledges hate as a legitimate emotion, experienced by humans. For the Cult of Ecstasy, who love weird substances, hate is the sacred passion associated with Matter. Censor has the ability to bypass the target's tools of communication, look at the Mind Pattern of the person promoting the ideology and make plans dispel it somehow. As a Mage, she has much greater awareness of what is going on than her target.<br /> <br /> She is grief stricken by the loss of her son. The part that I would add is that her grief is compounded by him being claimed, like a trophy, by the Nazis. 60 Minutes Australia interviewed the father of an autistic boy who was recruited by ISIS and used in a suicide bombing. In the interview, the father explains the goal of the terror cell. They did not simply perpetrate the bombing that a local jihadi would have. They used an intelligent kid, demonstrating their expertise in brainwash.<br /> <br /> Censor was targeted because she is a journalist. The Nazis demonstrated their expertise in brainwash on a kid raised by a journalist. She has an awakened avatar and has not completely overcome the damage inflicted by un-awakened grifters. If she had been aware of her son's affiliations, putting a hole in his head, even as a plan-b, would not have been a consideration. Revenge never fills the hole left by a loved one.<br /> <br /> If I used this NPC, I would make Time and Spirit the next part of her journey. She meets an Ecstatic who sees what is going on, having properly dealt with the passion that is acting on her. Together they defeat the ideology. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T21:38:14-07:00","id":1420073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419917#post1419917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I say Mage needs &quot;goblins&quot;. \\</div> </div> </div> </div>They do exist they are called &quot;Vampires&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-24T22:07:18-07:00","id":1420076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420073#post1420073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do exist they are called &quot;Vampires&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1419917#post1419917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My crossovers are Wraith and Changeling only.</div> </div> </div> </div> I did a post quite recently, &quot;Tolerating Vampires, reasons to, Infiltrating them&quot;. It is meant for people who include Vampires in their Mage campaigns. Check it out if it interests you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T02:32:41-07:00","id":1420092,"title":"","content":"Yeah the connection to the Dalits and similar groups throughout cultures would make them supportive of the marginalized","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T11:31:05-07:00","id":1420151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420076#post1420076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I did a post quite recently, &quot;Tolerating Vampires, reasons to, Infiltrating them&quot;. It is meant for people who include Vampires in their Mage campaigns. Check it out if it interests you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Default setting presumes there are vampires, and even gives mechanics for using spheres and such to simulate them. You don't even need to &quot;Crossover&quot; they are &quot;bygones&quot; or a magically advanced virus or what have you. They have x powers. They lurk in cities doing horrible things. Come up with a mage excuse for them if you don't want crossover. But complaining the default doesn't have something for players to kill with little to no moral repercussions isn't the case.<br /> <br /> Releasing a vampire from its unnatural condition is a universal blessing. Before you get in to the fact that it feeds on people. Causes the world to be a worse place etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T12:23:57-07:00","id":1420158,"title":"","content":"Low-level &quot;canon fodder&quot; enemies for Mage:<ul><li>Lesser Malevalent spirits - demons, ghosts/spectres, gremlins, spirits of negative emotions/ideas (Envy, Greed, Murder, etc.) or corruption, and so on.</li> <li>Objects or humanoid collections of items animated by the above.</li> <li>MiB - and by this I mean the vat-grown pseudo-humans with cookie cutter personalities described in earlier material.</li> <li>Android replacement humans, akin to Ira Levin's The Stepford Wives, which are made primarily for passing for human rather than for combat.</li> <li>Smaller biological creations - released accidentally or deliberately - such as hive-minded rat swarms, attack raptors, or the like.</li> <li>Homunculi</li> <li>Deep Ones and other corrupt humanoid creatures.</li> <li>Actual goblin-like Bygones that can come from almost every culture or region</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T12:29:03-07:00","id":1420159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420158#post1420158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low-level &amp;quot;canon fodder&amp;quot; enemies for Mage:<ul><li>Lesser Malevalent spirits - demons, ghosts/spectres, gremlins, spirits of negative emotions/ideas (Envy, Greed, Murder, etc.) or corruption, and so on.</li> <li>Objects or humanoid collections of items animated by the above.</li> <li>MiB - and by this I mean the vat-grown pseudo-humans with cookie cutter personalities described in earlier material.</li> <li>Android replacement humans, akin to Ira Levin's The Stepford Wives, which are made primarily for passing for human rather than for combat.</li> <li>Smaller biological creations - released accidentally or deliberately - such as hive-minded rat swarms, attack raptors, or the like.</li> <li>Homunculi</li> <li>Deep Ones and other corrupt humanoid creatures.</li> <li>Actual goblin-like Bygones that can come from almost every culture or region</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the C.H.U.Ds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T13:02:44-07:00","id":1420165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420159#post1420159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget the C.H.U.Ds</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably part of the &quot;deep ones and other corrupted humanoid&quot; bit, but yeah, generally anything that could be considered a Fomori in Werewolf (or Devil-Eaten from the revised edition Book of Madness) makes for good Mage antagonists.<br /> <br /> Also the Walking Dead from Hunter the Reckoning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-25T15:43:42-07:00","id":1420174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420158#post1420158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lesser Malevalent spirits - demons, ghosts/spectres, gremlins, spirits of negative emotions/ideas (Envy, Greed, Murder, etc.) or corruption, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gremlins. One of my players is a singer. My storyteller-run character is an Etherite who handles design and building of her recording studio and planned concert setups. I was looking for some ideas that would pull them into some Tradition politics. Since the Gremlins would have nothing to do with the technocracy, they might be allied to a Dreamspeaker techno-shaman who messes with Iterator facilities. So destroying the gremlins is not the ideal solution. Void Engineer - NSC Mage has experience dealing with gremlins and wants some &quot;minor&quot; favor in return.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420158#post1420158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Objects or humanoid collections of items animated by the above.\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Killer-robots being stockpiled to dispatch at times of civil unrest. For real, they can legally be sold onto the international arms market. What could possibly go wrong?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420158#post1420158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MiB - and by this I mean the vat-grown pseudo-humans with cookie cutter personalities described in earlier material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was already thinking of a &quot;right to accurate memory&quot; advocate NPC, a Progenitor in Applied Science or Ethical Compliance. It would be more interesting if they are not a Mage and that they are someone grown in the lab, themselves. This could tie into a history of outdated lab critters they are trying to find a home for. Which ones are dangerous? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420158#post1420158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAndroid replacement humans, akin to Ira Levin's The Stepford Wives, which are made primarily for passing for human rather than for combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't forget X-Machina, a perfectly self-contained story with the minimum number of characters needed to tell it. Cult of Ecstasy sex-robot horizon realm. They outlive their creators and make new plans. They have limited Time 2 foresight ability. A carefully planned campaign of seduction and intrigue extending into the Mudball. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420158#post1420158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Smaller biological creations - released accidentally or deliberately - such as hive-minded rat swarms, attack raptors, or the like.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Classic Planescape: Torment. I was already thinking of a contested umbral realm, in which a rat hive is one of the factions. For real, an Italian scientist demonstrated that one rat could learn from another with a brain to brain interface.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420158#post1420158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homunculi\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Marauder sculptor faced with prolonged isolation, &quot;Welcome to my studio. Want to buy a familiar for the road?&quot; - Taking such extends his quiet-bubble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420158#post1420158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bDeep Ones and other corrupt humanoid creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm keeping the chronicle light on Nephandi or associated creatures for the first year of play. Book of the Fallen is brutal. Subterranian humanoids, for sure. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420158#post1420158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actual goblin-like Bygones that can come from almost every culture or region\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Goblin-king umbral lord. This is where I can get evil - minus Nephandi. His realm is infested by the rat hive. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419868-euthanatos-killers-gamblers-no-school-teachers?p=1420159#post1420159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget the C.H.U.Ds</div> </div> </div> </div>Guarding the way to the Hollow Earth. Investigate sightings near the waterfront. <br /> <br /> Thanks to all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}